x706 text "editing"
x707 puts x705 x706
x708 call open x707 11
x709 write x708 2
x710 text "Views and edits"
x711 puts x709 x710
x712 call close x711 
x713 call open x712 2
x714 write x713 2
x715 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0) and, when the whole program matters, a program handle (g0) with one signature line per function. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line: `id op ...` replaces the instruction id or inserts it before ret; `id op ... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x` changes the result. Under g0, a whole `fn ... end` block adds or replaces a function and `-fn name` removes one. The edit is applied only if it parses, type-checks, validates, and was written against the current revision; otherwise it is rejected and the handle stays valid."
x716 puts x714 x715
x717 call close x716 
x718 call open x717 10
x719 write x718 4
x720 write x719 2
